    "summary": "Integration tests (code-review-divided.test.ts) drive runCodeReview end to end at a small limit and at a raised one: production runner, fold, record, dimension specs, adapters and s1's driver; judge slots mirror runDimensionJob with the test's limit (the configured limit lives in ~/.insrc); a scripted model judges only from what each call carries. Same verdicts per dimension and the same overall verdict both ways, each non-empty; cross-chunk contract mismatch reported at the caller; cross-chunk duplicate reported with counterpartRef; a degraded review whose coverage call is over the limit is divided with zero atoms (pipelineCalls chunk 0, one obligation per promised test) and judges each test on its evidence; an obligation answered at a note id twice fails the review with nothing written; every call within the limit.",
